{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merged: the end-to-end walkthrough's merge step, on main at 8f22ba52.\n\nThe walkthrough now captures the merged artifact's EventID, passes it as --rests-on before the positional supersede target, and audits the survivor rather than the artifact it has just retired. It also stops counting the reference's cases: it says the reference enumerates the situations, because a number here is a second copy of that table and drifts the moment the table changes — which is exactly what happened when splitting the rename case made four into six.\n\nThe flag ordering on this page is not a style preference. `gs supersede` prepends the target to the basis itself, so --rests-on carries the successor alone, and Go stops parsing flags at the first positional. The docset gate executes every command on this page, so both of those are verified rather than asserted.\n\nSuccessor at this path to 8d1051f8, the reviewed branch artifact.","body":{"commit":"8f22ba52cbe5921127e767395eadf1f8eff0db52","path":"docs/how-to/end-to-end.md"}}